X-SOURCE:Rancho Nicasio
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTSTAMP:20260904T180752
CREATED:20260819T173456Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T173504Z
UID:10000410-1788566400-1788652799@ranchonicasio.com
SUMMARY:MITCH POLZAK & THE ROYAL DEUCES
DESCRIPTION:DINNER SHOW WITH MITCH POLZAK & THE ROYAL DEUCES\nThe big guy from out West and larger than life energy (he’s also 6’5’) performer\, guitarist\, singer\, banjoist\, songwriter\, composer\, entertainer\, musical historian and teacher Mitch Polzak wears his heart on his sleeve and his playing in his heart. \nPolzak performs rockabilly and 60’s country music with the religious fervor of Jerry Lee Lewis and Johnny Cash and delivers a Honky Tonk ballad with the sincerity of Merle Haggard and Waylon Jennings. Mitch will bring a room to a fevered pitch of joyous energy on the dance floor and then tell you a story in a song like two old friends sitting at a kitchen table at midnight.
URL:https://ranchonicasio.com/event/mitch-polzak-the-royal-deuces-7/
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio\, 1 Old Rancheria Rd\, Nicasio\, CA\, 94946\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ranchonicasio.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Mitch-Polzak.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/seasons-turning-watercolor-basics"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Seasons Turning: Watercolor Basics  — Sebastopol Center For the 
 Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260905T000000
DTEND:20260906T000000
UID:f162395440cc3598659a74f27824923f@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nSeasons Turning: Waterco
 lor Basics\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $170.00\n        \n   
    \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, September 5th\, 2026 10AM - 4PMCost: $130 + $4
 0 materials feeWelcome the turning of the season with a day of watercolor 
 inspired bySonoma County in September—late summer tomatoes\, ripe figs a
 nd pears\,sunflowers\, dahlias\, peppers\, grapes\, and the rich colors of
  the changinglandscape. Earthy golds\, deep greens\, and dusty blues set t
 he tone forloose\, luminous paintings that capture the shift from summer i
 nto fall.Learn basic watercolor techniques including wet-on-wet painting\,
  controlledwashes\, layering\, color mixing\, and creating texture\, while
  building strongcompositions using color\, light\, and form. Guided discus
 sions explore theessential elements of visual art to help you create expre
 ssive\, individualwork.All materials provided. Space limited to 12 student
 s.Discussion break at 12:30 p.m. Please bring a brown bag lunch.About the 
 Instructor: Lynn Zachreson studied art at the University of Minnesota and 
 San Jose State University—Painting\, Printmaking: BA Fine Art. She has e
 xperience teaching all ages: Watercolor painting skills\, 30+ years\, Wate
 rcolor figure painting 20+ years\, and Fine Art Basics with Mixed Media 20
 + years. Lynn enjoys spending her time painting\, teaching\, long distance
  hiking\, and gardening. View Lynn’s art here: https://lynnzachresonart.
 com/\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            Reserve Your Spot
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/seasons-turning-watercolor-ba
 sics
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
