SUMMARY:TRJG plays for Death and Taxes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T000000
UID:260813eaWDqhX2nkWPTeDj2Q4poQ
DESCRIPTION:TRJG is the one-man-band project of Drew Clinard. He plays liv
 ely\, family-friendly\, original Americana/Alt-Country. Covers include Bob
  Dylan\, Gillian Welch\, Lucinda Williams\, Neil Young\, John Prine. \n\nD
 rew spent years off-grid honing his craft mixing up old-time traditionals 
 and writing songs inspired by hard times and good times. His most successf
 ul musical endeavor prior to TRJG was the Americana group Cuyama Mama & th
 e Hot Flashes. \n\nHis first record\, Goodbye Home\, was released in COVID
 -2020 - so fun! More music out now - https://therealjohngary.bandcamp.com/
 \n\nCatch TRJG at The Sailing Goat in Pt. Richmond\, Headlands Brewing Laf
 ayette\, Berkeley farmers' markets\, etc.
LOCATION:Moonlight Brewing Company
