SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T170000
UID:260903v5laBroCAEaKk6gMVqIioA
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, Lucci Lambrusco is taking over 
 Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen\, bringing a taste of Italian aperitivo
  culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afternoon o
 f Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made for
  lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined every
  Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and producers
 \, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more abou
 t what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on Thursday\, September
  3\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancini on the
  patio.\n\nLUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER Monday–Friday | 3:00–
 5:00 PM September & October\n\nTHURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES Every Thursday |
  3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptember 10 | Oliver 
 McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24 | Idlewild Wine
 s\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti Vineyards\n\nOct
 ober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\nLucci is pouring all season 
 long\, with a few friends joining along the way.\n\nCome for a glass. Stay
  for another.\n\nJOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/belongings-bringing-memories-to-life/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:BELONGINGS: Bringing Memories to Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T180000
UID:2609043LinKut3P0CusOWhjjQBnw
DESCRIPTION:A Creative Workshop on Memory\, Grief & Storytelling Facilitat
 ed by Filmmaker Danièle Wilmouth\n\nSaturday\, September 5\, 3-6 pm\n\nPe
 taluma Historical Library & Museum\n\n20 4th Street \\(Corner of 4th & B S
 treet\\)\n\nRegistration:  $30 per person\n\n• Limited to 12 participan
 ts\n\n• Light snacks will be provided.\n\nWhat do we do with the things 
 our loved ones leave behind? \n\nJoin award-winning filmmaker Danièle Wil
 mouth for an intimate\, three-hour workshop exploring how meaningful objec
 ts can become powerful vessels for memory\, healing\, and creative express
 ion. \n\nDrawing from her own artistic practice\, Danièle will share how 
 she uses photographs\, letters\, family documents\, music\, treasured obje
 cts\, and stop-motion animation to honor loved ones and transform personal
  stories into lasting works of art. \n\nParticipants are invited to bring
  one to three meaningful objects that hold a special memory or story. Th
 rough film excerpts\, guided conversation\, and creative brainstorming\, y
 ou’ll explore ways to preserve family history through storytelling\, wri
 ting\, journaling\, archival materials\, and simple stop-motion animation 
 techniques. No filmmaking or artistic experience is necessary—just curio
 sity and a willingness to reflect. \n\nWhether you’re looking to preserv
 e family memories\, process grief\, or discover new creative ways to tell 
 your story\, this workshop offers a welcoming space for reflection\, conne
 ction\, and inspiration. \n\nThis workshop is presented in conjunction wit
 h Belongings: What We Bring\, What We Leave Behind\, on view September 4
 –October 4\, 2026\, at the Petaluma Historical Library & Museum. The exh
 ibition explores migration\, memory\, and belonging through the treasured 
 objects and personal stories that connect us across generations. \n\nBelon
 gings: What We Bring\, What We Leave Behind is made possible through the 
 generous support of California Humanities through its Connecting Califo
 rnia grant program. We are also deeply grateful to our community partners
  and sponsors\, including the North Bay Asian American Pacific Islander C
 oalition\, Sonoma County Japanese American Citizens League\, Petaluma Ar
 ts Center\, Life on Art\, Zimbabwe Cultural Exchange Project of Californ
 ia\, El Día de los Muertos Petaluma\, Bolca Avia\, Chelsea Antiques\,
  Café Puente\, Rustic Bakery\, Quality Inn Petaluma\, and all of the o
 rganizations\, volunteers\, artists\, and community members whose collabor
 ation has brought this exhibition to life. \n\n 
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library and Museum
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/belongings-bringing-memo
 ries-to-life/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
