BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest", "Press Democrat": "https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Tomales Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:260826SvckaKk0bES8ecd39IdCJg
DESCRIPTION:The Tomales Festival will be held at High Noon on Labor Day Su
 nday\, September 6th. Join us in the Community Park \\(in between the Cath
 olic church and the William Tell House\\) to celebrate with friends and ne
 ighbors. This year we're featuring music by the Blues Defenders\, plus fre
 sh oysters\, beer\, wine\, food\, and drink. Local arts and crafts\, plus 
 displays from local organizations and non-profits.\n\nThe festival is \\(a
 nd always has been\\) created\, organized\, and carried out by volunteers 
 from the local community. This local tradition has quite a history: it was
  the Swiss-Italian celebration from 1888 until 1994\, when it became Found
 er's Day and later the Tomales Festival. That's 138 years worth of parades
 \, picnics\, and parties. This event benefits the Tomales Town Hall\, whic
 h is a 501\\(c\\)3 non-profit community center.\n\nSpecial thanks to Kathr
 yn LeMieux for once again allowing us to use her whimsical cow painting as
  our festive logo. And thanks to our contributors. The Hog Island Oyster C
 ompany and The Marshall Store contributed the shellfish. Morris Distributi
 ng is providing our beer supply. Recology Sonoma/Marin is providing trash 
 containers and is donating garbage service. We are grateful to our sponsor
  Marin Agricultural Land Trust \\(MALT\\).\n\nSign ups for volunteers\, e
 xhibitors\, vendors\, and more right are currently available. Write to fes
 tival@TomalesTownHall.org or see the website: https://www.tomalestownhall.
 org/tomalesfest. Booth reservations end August 15th.
LOCATION:Tomales Community Park
URL:https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mareislandartstudios.com/events/nothing-to-see-here-jason-perry/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Nothing To See Here - Jason Perry
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T160000
UID:260830jdYuVnR5wEWjapehr1aFHg
DESCRIPTION:"Nothing To See Here" is a critical\, yet playful examination 
 of the UFO phenomenon that is hinged on the dynamic between serious scient
 ific inquiry and fringe science.\n\nWith a mixed media approach that combi
 nes drawing\, collage\, and painting\, Jason Perry seeks to entice the vie
 wer into the work through familiar visual iconography\, bold colors\, expr
 essive marks\, and textures. Once there\, the viewer is offered a deeper l
 ayer of meaning to consider. Perry calls into question the blurred narrati
 ves\, misinformation\, and potential truths surrounding the UFO topic.\n\n
 At its core\, "Nothing To See Here" invites us to look a little closer at 
 our beliefs\, our relationship to the strange\, the unexplained\, and our 
 enduring fascination with what might be out there.
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://mareislandartstudios.com/events/nothing-to-see-here-jason-perr
 y/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
