SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041939Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T100000
SUMMARY:Outdoor Pranayama
DESCRIPTION:Nataraja School of Traditional Yoga\n**Morning Pranayama - Tra
 ditional Yogic Breathwork with Kara Weimer**\n**Tuesdays 9-10am**\n\\*\\*R
 SVP ONLY - \\*Certain injuries & health issues may be contraindicated - Pl
 ease contact me if you have a concern \\*\\*\\*\n\nStart your morning with
  traditional yogic breathwork with the added benefits of sunshine\, fresh 
 air and grounding. It is ideal to practice pranayama outside.\n\nPranayama
  is distinct from modern breathwork. It is an important component & taught
  in context to the process of yoga. Designed to harness prana (life force 
 energy)\, purify & balance the nadis (channels) & awaken subtle energy for
  physical\, mental\, and spiritual development. Not limited to just well-b
 eing. Not a quick fix or forceful temporary cathartic experiences\, but ta
 ught as a safe & gradual process requiring discipline & consistency.\n\nRe
 lease toxins\, clear and align the energy channels\, strengthen the lungs\
 , massage\, tone & nourish internal organs\, strengthen agni & digestion\,
  oxygenate and improve blood flow\, strengthen immunity & clear the mind. 
 Implement various techniques to purify\, energize\, focus & calm the mind 
 & nervous system & harness the vital life force energy - with kumbhaka & b
 andha (breath holds and internal locks). Known to increase neuroplasticity
 \, nitric oxide\, and erase old mental and emotional patterns. Traditional
 ly\, pranayama is the doorway to access higher states of consciousness.\n\
 nThroughout the ongoing class different practices will be presented. Learn
  Cleansing kriyas\, Himalayan Pranayama including including Ujjayi Variati
 ons\, Heating & Cooling Breaths\, Solar\, Lunar & Soli-Lunar Nadi Shuddhi 
 practices\, Samantraka Pranayama\, Mudra\, Pratyahara\, Subtle & Contempla
 tive Practices. Includes Pranava techniques for contemplation and merging 
 with the vibration and sound of Om and Nada - internal sound current.\n\nK
 ara is a long time practitioner & teacher- trained extensively with Himala
 yan yoga adepts in advanced pranayama & mudra using the breath as the guid
 e for transformation and self-empowerment. With deep knowledge of pranayam
 a\, she safely guides practitioners progressively.\n\nPlease practice on a
 n empty stomach. Please bring a mat or blanket and a cushion or folded bla
 nket to sit on. Please wear layers.\nRagle Ranch Park\, Sebastopol\nRSVP -
  $20 - Discounted Class Series'\, Sliding Scale Available\nContact Kara 70
 7-235-1413\nsunyogadance@gmail.com
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nataraja-school-of-traditional-yoga/e
 vents/316183390/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260819T160810Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T160810Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopolcalendar": "https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/outdoor-traditional-pranayama/2026-09-08/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebastopolcalendar
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Calendar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T100000
DTSTAMP:20260528T140541Z
CREATED:20260528T140541Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260528T140541Z
UID:10008383-1788858000-1788861600@sebastopolcalendar.com
SUMMARY:Outdoor Traditional Pranayama
DESCRIPTION:Morning Pranayama – Traditional Yogic Breathwork with Kara Weimer\nTuesdays 9-10am\n**RSVP ONLY – *Certain injuries & health issues may be contraindicated – Please contact me if you have a concern *** \nStart your morning with traditional yogic breathwork with the benefits of practicing in the peace of nature\, fresh air & sunshine. \nPranayama is distinct from modern breathwork. It is an important component & taught in context to the process of yoga. Designed to harness prana (life force energy)\, purify & balance the nadis (energy channels)\, awaken subtle energy & still the mind. Not limited to just well-being. Not a quick fix or forceful temporary cathartic experiences\, but taught as a safe & gradual process requiring discipline & consistency. \nRelease toxins\, clear and align the energy channels\, strengthen the lungs\, massage\, tone & nourish internal organs\, strengthen agni & digestion\, oxygenate and improve blood flow\, strengthen immunity & clear the mind. Implement various techniques to purify\, energize\, focus & calm the mind & nervous system & harness the vital life force energy – with kumbhaka & bandha (breath holds and internal locks). Known to increase neuroplasticity\, nitric oxide\, and erase old mental and emotional patterns. Traditionally\, pranayama is the doorway to access higher states of consciousness. \nThroughout the ongoing class different practices will be presented. Learn Cleansing kriyas\, Himalayan Pranayama including including Ujjayi Variations\, Heating & Cooling Breaths\, Solar\, Lunar & Soli-Lunar Nadi Shuddhi practices\, Samantraka Pranayama\, Mudra\, Pratyahara\, Subtle & Contemplative Practices. Includes Pranava techniques for contemplation and merging with the vibration and sound of Om and Nada – internal sound current. \nKara is a long time practitioner & teacher- trained extensively with Himalayan yoga adepts in advanced pranayama\, mudra & meditation using the breath as the guide for transformation and self-empowerment. With deep knowledge of pranayama\, she safely guides practitioners progressively. \nPlease practice on an empty stomach. Please bring a mat or blanket and a cushion or folded blanket to sit on. Please wear layers.\nRagle Ranch Park\, Sebastopol\nRSVP – $20 – Discounted Class Series’\, Sliding Scale Available\nContact Kara 707-235-1413\nsunyogadance@gmail.com
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/outdoor-traditional-pranayama/2026-09-08/
LOCATION:Ragle Ranch Regional Park\, 500 Ragle Road\, Sebastopol\, CA\, 95472\, United States
CATEGORIES:Exercise/Yoga,Spiritual
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/outdoorpranayama-1.png
ORGANIZER;CN="NatarajaSchoolof Traditional Yoga":MAILTO:sunyogadance@gmail.com
GEO:38.4052061;-122.8453567
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Ragle Ranch Regional Park 500 Ragle Road Sebastopol CA 95472 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=500 Ragle Road:geo:-122.8453567,38.4052061
END:VEVENT
