BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23865-research-remix-find-research-cite-it-right-with"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research + Cite It Right with NoodleTools
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T160000
DTSTAMP:20260827T150443Z
UID:20260909T220000Z-23865@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T150000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliogr
 aphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\,
  including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs. This workshop w
 ill use the MLA citation style\, which is typically used in the English\, 
 ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines.  If you are usin
 g APA\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose this option in Noo
 dleTools too.  You will learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleToo
 ls. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\, create a bi
 bliography and check for errors.  Along the way\, you will receive quick t
 ips on how to find credible research in the library and on the web.  Extra
  Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and c
 ourse name when you register if you would like us to notify your instructo
 r that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work 
 with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your att
 endance.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T173021Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23865-research-remix-find-researc
 h-cite-it-right-with
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA 
 citations and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and pa
 per-writing features\, including the capability to create papers via Googl
 eDocs. This workshop will use the MLA citation style\, which is typically 
 used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion discipl
 ines.</p><p>  If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how
  to choose this option in NoodleTools too.</p><p>  You will learn how to s
 ign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show h
 ow to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.</p><p
 >  Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible res
 earch in the library and on the web.</p><p>  Extra Credit: As students\, y
 ou have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you regi
 ster if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended
  the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on 
 an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:23865
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80
 /height/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1080\,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour
 .rev.1786057687.png
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
END:VEVENT
