SUMMARY:Quench at Copia: Sonoma Leadership & Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T183000
UID:260905AizhrYM5lEWjDNErPz64UA
DESCRIPTION:Sip and learn Sonoma’s Leadership and Legacy with host and M
 aster Sommelier Andrea Immer Robinson plus special guest sommelier\, educa
 tor\, and consultant Christopher Sawyer. Together\, they’ll explore the 
 stories\, wines\, and enduring influence of two iconic Sonoma County wine 
 families\, Hanzell Vineyards and Bacigalupi Vineyards. With every pour\, e
 njoy custom “Taste of The Grove” gourmet bites designed to complement 
 the wines and bring their tasting notes to life. \n\nWines included: \n\
 n2011 Hanzell “Ambassador” Chardonnay\, Estate Grown\, Sonoma Valley *
 (in 1.5L magnums)* \n\n2017 Bacigalupi Chardonnay\, Estate Grown\, Russia
 n River Valley \n\n2023 Hanzell “Heritage” Chardonnay\, Estate Grown\
 , Moon Mountain District \n\n2023 Bacigalupi “Renouveau” Chardonnay\,
  Estate Grown\, Russian River Valley \n\n2021 Hanzell “The Maggie's Sel
 ection” Pinot Noir\, Estate Grown\, Moon Mountain District \n\n2022 Bac
 igalupi Pinot Noir\, Pommard Clone\, Estate Grown\, Russian River Valley 
 \n\nReserve your seat and raise a glass to the families who helped shape i
 t!
LOCATION:CIA at Copia
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/quench-at-copia-sonoma-leadership-legacy-
 tickets-1997723467669
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
