X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net", "Press Democrat": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
UID:2607153_nzdtHax02kZ-ZaQJ0H6w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brandlin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-brandlin-estate-wine-food-tasting-experience/18318441/2026-09-10T11"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brandlin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T160000
UID:260312ggmH64miK06QN3fS26LxLQ
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Brandlin Estate 
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brand
 lin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/", "Press Democrat": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T170000
UID:260430Vj-PvQ3xLkWjcO6HhDx0oA
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
