SUMMARY:Opening Reception - Tom Chown: 46 Years Behind the Lens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
DTSTAMP:20260825T094521Z
UID:20260910T230000Z-23757@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T160000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1000,1000/689_cs_-_Tom_Chown_Photo_Exhibit.rev.17876
 76636.jpg
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the camp
 us photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he became a familiar presence
  throughout the college community\, documenting the people\, programs and 
 milestones that shaped generations of students and employees.  The exhibit
 ion will trace Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from working with fil
 m and developing photographs in the darkroom to embracing digital photogra
 phy. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nea
 rly five decades of college life.  A selection of photographs in the exhib
 it will be available for bidding\, with 100% of the proceeds benefiting th
 e SRJC Foundation's Jeanne Chown Memorial Nursing Scholarship. Established
  in 1998 in honor of Chown's mother\, the scholarship supports students pu
 rsuing careers in nursing.Location: Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle 
 Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa CampusFor more information\, visit SRJC's R
 obert F. Agrella Art Gallery website. (https://art-gallery.santarosa.edu/e
 xhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260825T165703Z
LOCATION:Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23757-opening-reception-tom-chown
 -46-years-behind-the-lens
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24
 \, working in the campus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he beca
 me a familiar presence throughout the college community\, documenting the 
 people\, programs and milestones that shaped generations of students and e
 mployees.</p><p>  The exhibition will trace Chown's evolution as a photogr
 apher\, from working with film and developing photographs in the darkroom 
 to embracing digital photography. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\
 , preserving moments from nearly five decades of college life.</p><p>  A s
 election of photographs in the exhibit will be available for bidding\, wit
 h 100% of the proceeds benefiting the SRJC Foundation's Jeanne Chown Memor
 ial Nursing Scholarship. Established in 1998 in honor of Chown's mother\, 
 the scholarship supports students pursuing careers in nursing.</p><p><stro
 ng>Location:</strong> Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle Library 1st fl
 oor - Santa Rosa Campus</p><p><a href="https://art-gallery.santarosa.edu/e
 xhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more
  information\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery website.</a></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:23757
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80
 /height/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1000\,1000/689_cs_-_Tom_Chown_Photo_Exh
 ibit.rev.1787676636.jpg
