BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-linocut/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T130000
UID:260823tUPxq5oiIE64LL9uQ2mxUw
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. Please note: This class requires ha
 nd dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel comfor
 table standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/how-to-be-ok-with-an-overwhelmed-mind-coming-home-to-the-wisdom-of-the-body-lb1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/how-to-be-ok-with-an-overwhelmed-mind-coming-home-to-the-wisdom-of-the-body-lb1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/how-to-be-ok-with-an-overwhelmed-mind-coming-home-to-the-wisdom-of-the-body-lb1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:How to be OK with an Overwhelmed Mind
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T150000
UID:2608172sYGRjLM-0WCwqT-tsU1jg
DESCRIPTION:with Leslie Booker\n\nLet’s first debunk the myth that our m
 ind should be completely quiet and empty of all thoughts. This is a high b
 ar to meet during our meditation practice\, and certainly not the reality 
 of a healthy mind. Just as the tongue tastes and the nose smells\, the min
 d thinks… it’s its job! The goal of meditation is not about how quiet
  and still our mind (and body) can get\, but how we respond to a mind that
  is overwhelmed\, creative\, anxious\, dreamy\, neurodiverse\, and even a 
 little sleepy.\n\nAnd we do this by allowing the wisdom of the body to tak
 e the lead.\n\nThis day is not meant to exclude\, pathologize\, or diagnos
 e anyone\, but to normalize that there is a lot happening in the mind\, an
 d explore how mindfulness of the body can support us in untangling and reg
 ulating the nervous system to reduce some of that anxiety.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/how-to-be-ok-with-an-o
 verwhelmed-mind-coming-home-to-the-wisdom-of-the-body-lb1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
