SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T000000
UID:260813sfOVW3C5TkG1AFjhBgPFNA
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:The Backdrop (Indulge Sonoma Event)
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108677372?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/", "Press Democrat": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacific/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T170000
UID:260803eEGVuASYnUyALvBG9mxtdw
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
