SUMMARY:2nd Annual BEE in Kenya Dinner and Art Auction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T210000
UID:260817u0VPodwNf061ZiB6yEudDw
DESCRIPTION:Healdsburg\, CA — \\[Sept. 12\\] — Following the incredibl
 e success of its first sold-out and waitlisted Bee-Inspired Benefit Dinner
  at Preston Farm and Winery and first BEE in Kenya dinner at Acorn\, Sonom
 a County Bee Company is thrilled to announce their third dinner experience
  and Second Annual BEE in Kenya Benefit Dinner—an unforgettable evening 
 celebrating community\, conservation\, and global connection.\n\nOn \\[Sep
 t 12\\]\, guests are invited to gather at Dragonfly Floral in Healdsburg f
 or a community-driven fundraising dinner benefiting Bee in Kenya\, the non
 profit co-founded by beekeeper and Sonoma County Bee Company owner Candice
  Koseba.\n\nThis year's event will also feature an all-art auction\, with 
 original works generously donated by an inspiring collection of local and 
 international artists. Local artists Jake Messing\, Jessica Martin\, and S
 ebastian Pochan to name a few. Each piece has been donated to help raise c
 ritical funds for BEE in Kenya's mission\, making art an integral part of 
 an evening dedicated to creating meaningful impact.\n\nBEE in Kenya 501\\(
 c\\)\\(3\\)—short for Beekeepers and Educators Engaged in Kenya—works 
 to empower rural Kenyan communities through ecological education and susta
 inable beekeeping. The organization partners with schools and community or
 ganizations throughout Kenya to foster a deeper understanding of natural e
 cosystems\, the essential role of bees\, and regenerative beekeeping pract
 ices that support environmental stewardship and long-term economic resilie
 nce.\n\nEvery ticket purchased\, every auction bid\, and every donation ma
 de directly supports BEE in Kenya's programs\, helping provide beekeeping 
 equipment\, training\, educational resources\, and opportunities that stre
 ngthen both communities and the landscapes they depend on.\n\nAs Sonoma Ma
 gazine noted in its coverage of previous events: 🔗 “An Upcoming Winer
 y Dinner in Healdsburg Is Creating a Lot of Buzz”\n\nAll proceeds from t
 he dinner will directly support BEE in Kenya’s initiatives\, including e
 quipment grants for rural beekeepers\, curriculum development for schools\
 , and training workshops in sustainable apiculture.\n\nTickets are limited
  — and if history is any indication\, they’ll sell fast. Be part of th
 e buzz and help bring the transformative power of bees across continents.\
 n\nEvent Details 📍 Location: Dragonfly Floral \\+ Farm : 425 Westside R
 d\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448 📅 Date: Saturday September 12 6-9pm 🎟 Tick
 ets:2nd Annual BEE in Kenya Benefit Dinner & Art Auction
LOCATION:Dragonfly Floral
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/2nd-annual-bee-in-kenya-benefit-dinner-ar
 t-auction-tickets-1996131096845?discount=ARTISTPRICE2026&keep_tld=true
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
