SUMMARY:Movie Night: Grease
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T220000
UID:260528b-JGZxd8bE6lAwrkXQc5jg
DESCRIPTION:Movie Night: Grease\n\nPublic Event\n\nFriday\, September 18\,
  2026\n\n5-10 p.m. • All Ages • No Pets Allowed\n\n**Schedule:**\n\n·
          **Classic Car Show:** 5-7 p.m. *(free\, open to the publi
 c)*\n\n·         **Meet and Greet with Kelly Ward of “Grease”
 :** 6:30-7:30 p.m. *(ticket holders only)*\n\n·         **Movie S
 creening:** 7:30-10 p.m. *(ticket holders only)*\n\nMovie Night on the Law
 n is getting a retro twist! Join us for a family-friendly evening inspired
  by classic 1950s cruise-night fun\, featuring a screening of Grease under
  the stars.\n\nBefore the movie begins\, stroll through a pre-show classic
  car display\, enjoy juicy burgers\, and sip your favorite Dry Creek Viney
 ard wines. We’re thrilled to welcome actor Kelly Ward\, beloved for his 
 role as T-Bird Putzie in the film\, for a special appearance.\n\nGuests of
  all ages are encouraged to dress up and lean into the era — whether you
 ’re channeling Danny or Sandy\, rolling in with the T-Birds\, sparkling 
 with the Pink Ladies\, or putting your own vintage spin on it. Prizes for 
 standout costumes will be awarded!\n\n **Tickets:** $40 per person
LOCATION:Dry Creek Vineyard
URL:https://www.drycreekvineyard.com/events/page/3/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://events.humanitix.com/sqff-healing-through-hula", "Press Democrat": "https://events.humanitix.com/sqff-healing-through-hula"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://events.humanitix.com/sqff-healing-through-hula"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:SQFF & International Day of Peace Festival present : Healing Throu
 gh Hula
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T203000
UID:260831xpFe41S2SES7Z9JbD8YWaA
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center's International Day 
 of Peace Festival weekend begins with a special screening of the document
 ary feature Healing Through Hula\, presented by the San Quentin Film Fes
 tival. The film sets the tone for a weekend dedicated to exploring the man
 y pathways to peace.\n\nDirected by Louis Sále\, Healing Through Hula t
 ells the powerful story of Asian American and Pacific Islander men in pris
 on who reconnect with their cultural heritage through the practice of hula
 . Drawing from his own lived experience\, Sále chronicles a journey of he
 aling and redemption that culminates in a moving Makahiki ceremonial ritua
 l. The original 10-minute version of the film was first screened at the in
 augural San Quentin Film Festival \\(SQFF\\) in 2024\, where it received t
 he award for Best Documentary Short. The evening program will include two
  additional short films: Processing\, a SQFF25 Short Film Finalist\, direc
 ted by formerly incarcerated filmmaker\, artist and musician Antwan Banks
  Williamsand Exonerated\, directed by incarcerated filmmaker Ernest “Be
 n Shua”Woods II. \n\nFollowing the film\, attendees are invited to stay
  for a panel discussion featuring director Antwan Williams and Demora He
 nderson\, the subject of Exonerated\, who was released in June and contin
 ues the struggle to overturn his wrongful conviction. The conversation wil
 l be moderated by the Community Center's own Alexa Davidson.\n\nPrior to 
 the screening\, at 5:30pm guests are invited to enjoy a reception where t
 he Lagunitas Middle School eighth-grade class will offer refreshments as a
  fundraiser for their Spring 2027 Civil Rights Field Trip.\n\nHealing Thro
 ugh Hula begins at 6:30pm sharp!
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://events.humanitix.com/sqff-healing-through-hula
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
