SUMMARY:Healdsburg Repair Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T130000
UID:2608290ubFumCLj0SvU-Np4eXznQ
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\nBring it to the Repair Fair!‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and spe
 cialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair\\* your items.  
 We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so you can le
 arn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods\, and e
 ven how to repair things yourself!  \n\nIf you’d like to bring an it
 em to repair\, please register the item here: https://www.reusealliance.or
 g/rf-reg\n\n\\(Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your item!\\)\n\nT
 his event will also include a Clothing Swap! Bring clothing and accessorie
 s to share and take home something new-to-you. Please limit donations to 1
  bag per person \\(clean and good condition only\, no undergarments or soc
 ks please\\)\, but take as much as you’d like! More about clothing swaps
  here.\n\nThis is a free public event.
LOCATION:Abel de Luna Community Center
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/healdsburg-repairfair
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/heirloom-apple-festival", "Press Democrat": "https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/heirloom-apple-festival"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/heirloom-apple-festival"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Heirloom Apple Festival at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T150000
UID:260828Sj6OHsSZlUK4PBr3gKpQSQ
DESCRIPTION:Experience the magic and heritage of heirloom apples at Gold R
 idge Organic Farms' Fifth Annual Heirloom Apple Festival in Sebastopol. Th
 is family-friendly day honors the wonderful\, diverse\, and delicious heir
 loom apple varieties grown in our organic orchards\, as well as the region
 's rich agricultural history.\n\nFeaturing curated tastes of a handful of 
 our 70+ heirloom apple varieties grown onsite in our organic orchards and 
 our organic Extra Virgin Olive Oils. Plus\, enjoy local cheese and apple p
 airings\, our award-winning apple cider balsamic vinegar and beloved apple
  cider syrup.\n\nStroll through our beautiful olive and apple orchards wit
 h founder-farmer Brooke Hazen or take a ride on our apple-themed trolley. 
 Enjoy a sample of our own freshly pressed apple juice from our hand-turned
  cider press. Spark your curiosity with culinary adventures\, cooking demo
 s\, and displays. Kids can win a prize on an apple-themed scavenger hunt. 
 Plus\, Goatlandia will be here with some special friends to say hello!\n\n
 Local Producers & Friends:\n\nMeet the makers: this year we're celebrating
  local producers who share our passion for honest\, heritage food. Join us
  in welcoming Kiss the Flower Honey Co\, KM Mushrooms\, Blooming Fields Fa
 rm\, and our friend and neighbor\, Larry the Tomato Guy. Each will be samp
 ling their products and sharing more about their farms. \n\nFood & Refres
 hments:\n\nWood-fired pizzas by Chef Seamus (11:00 AM–2:30 PM or until s
 old out)—order in advance or a la carte. Also available: locally made ap
 ple crumble (made with our own apples\, of course) and delicious apple cid
 er slushies.\n\nEntertainment:\n\nLive music by Spike Sikes and his Awesom
 e Hotcakes!\n\nAll activities take place outside\, around our olive press 
 or on the crush pad.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/heirloom-apple-festival
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-linocut/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T130000
UID:2608235jTR4hH4eESMKAiPnoXXgg
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. Please note: This class requires ha
 nd dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel comfor
 table standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
