X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Novel Lovers Of Sebastopol": "https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/315204096/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_novel_lovers_of_sebastopol
X-SOURCE:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County
UID:event_315204096@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041942Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T143000
SUMMARY:The Things We Never Say by Elizabeth Strout [OPTION 1]
DESCRIPTION:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County\, CA\nPublisher's description: A
 rtie Dam is living a double life. He spends his days teaching history to e
 leventh graders\, expanding their young minds\, correcting their casual cr
 uelties\, and lending a kind word to those who need it most. He goes to ho
 liday parties with his wife of three decades\, makes small talk with neigh
 bors\, and\, on weekends\, takes his sailboat out on the beautiful Massach
 usetts Bay. He is\, by all appearances\, present and alive. But inside\, A
 rtie is plagued by feelings of isolation. He looks out at a world gone mad
 —at himself and the people around him—and turns a question over and ov
 er in his mind: How is it that we know so little about one another\, even 
 those closest to us?\n\nAnd then\, one day\, Artie learns that life has be
 en keeping a secret from him\, one that threatens to upend his entire worl
 d. Once he learns it\, he is forced to chart a new course\, to reconsider 
 the relationships he holds most dear—and to make peace with the mysterie
 s at the heart of our existence.\n\nElizabeth Strout\, as we have come to 
 expect\, delivers a moving exploration of the human condition—one that b
 rims with compassion for each and every one of her indelible characters. W
 ith exquisite prose and profound insight\, *The Things We Never Say* takes
  one man’s fears and loneliness and makes them universal. And in the sam
 e breath\, captures the abiding love that sustains and holds us all.\n\n"I
  haven't enjoyed a Strout book this much in years. Strout takes you inside
  Artie\, gradually revealing pieces of his past and his relationships. Des
 pite the premise\, much of the book is upbeat\, and when it isn't\, we're 
 rooting for Artie." - Joan\n\n"More wonderful characters and interesting n
 arrative from Strout. Highly recommend." - Dave\n\n"I too\, am a fan of *T
 he Things We Never Say.* I was immediately drawn into this novel. Can't wa
 it!"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/315
 204096/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260610T221022Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T221022Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
