SUMMARY:Sierra Winds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T150000
UID:260820kWhHR5jTGUqepYp4jVqj4g
DESCRIPTION:The United States Air Force Band of the Golden West is station
 ed in the San Francisco Bay Area at Travis Air Force Base. The only active
  duty Air Force band west of the Rockies\, the Band of the Golden West is 
 comprised of 60 talented and versatile Airmen-musicians under the command 
 of Captain Brian O'Donnell. In addition to performing for civilian communi
 ties throughout the states of Washington\, Oregon\, California\, Arizona\,
  and Nevada\, the band supports 13 Air Force Bases and 8 Air Force Reserve
  Wings in over 400 performances annually for 9 million listeners. The orga
 nization offers several outstanding performing groups\; The Concert Band\,
  Ceremonial Marching Band\, The Commanders Jazz Ensemble\, Mobility Rock B
 and\, Galaxy Rock Band\, Sierra Winds\, Golden West Winds\, Travis Brass Q
 uintet\, Golden West Brass Band\, and more. Additionally\, the Band of the
  Golden West provides solo musicians for performances of the National Anth
 em and solo buglers for Taps details. The band has performed with musical 
 artists such as Arturo Sandoval\, Pentatonix\, the San Francisco Symphony\
 , the Hollywood Bowl Orchestra\, and with notable organizations such as th
 e San Francisco 49ers\, the Arizona Cardinals\, NASCAR\, The Tournament of
  Roses Parade\, and many many more.
LOCATION:Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17116732
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
