X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomapeaceintheplaza.org/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/peace-in-the-plaza/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomapeaceintheplaza.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomapeaceintheplaza.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Peace in the Plaza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T173000
UID:260830cgCpzTGqRkeaPZ9_6naKWQ
DESCRIPTION:Peace in the Plaza is a public event inspired by the United Na
 tions International Day of Peace and presented by Sonoma Ashram. This free
  half-day event will include live music\, ongoing yoga classes\, a wellnes
 s hub\, children’s activities\, and community tabling. The event will be
  presented in partnership with local civic\, faith\, and wellness leaders.
  Musicians will include Sukhawat Ali Khan Band\, Vox Populi\, Sophia Sanch
 ez\, and René Jenkins.\n\nAs part of the opening ceremony\, there will be
  a minute of silence at 12 PM to coincide with the UN International Day of
  Peace moment of silence around the world. Guided meditations and an after
 noon talk will be provided by Sonoma Ashram Founder Baba Harihar Ramji\, a
 ffectionately known as “Babaji." Babaji has inspired people in the Sonom
 a Valley for over 35 years. His teachings emphasize living simply\, inner 
 freedom\, and selfless service.\n\nThe intention is to inspire our communi
 ty to remember the inner peace within us all—because true peace begins a
 t home and expands naturally to our families\, neighborhoods\, and the wor
 ld.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://sonomapeaceintheplaza.org/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T160000
UID:260629mL8GuYIe_km2Br-oV-Islg
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
