SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research + Cite It Right with NoodleTools
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T180000
DTSTAMP:20260827T152648Z
UID:20260922T000000Z-23871@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T170000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliogr
 aphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\,
  including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.  This NoodleToo
 ls workshop will use the MLA citation style\, which is typically used in t
 he English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines. If 
 you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose this o
 ption in NoodleTools too.  You will learn how to sign up for an account wi
 th NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\,
  create a bibliography and check for errors. Along the way\, you will rece
 ive quick tips on how to find credible research in the library and on the 
 web.  Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style appropriate
  for your research assignment.  Extra Credit: As students\, you have the o
 ption to submit your instructor and course name when you register if you w
 ould like us to notify your instructor that you have attended the workshop
  for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternativ
 e way to provide evidence of your attendance.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T175143Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23871-research-remix-find-researc
 h-cite-it-right-with
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA 
 citations and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and pa
 per-writing features\, including the capability to create papers via Googl
 eDocs.</p><p>  This NoodleTools workshop will use the MLA citation style\,
  which is typically used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, 
 and Religion disciplines. If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We wi
 ll share how to choose this option in NoodleTools too.</p><p>  You will le
 arn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide exampl
 es to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for e
 rrors. Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible
  research in the library and on the web.</p><p>  Check with your instructo
 r to confirm the citation style appropriate for your research assignment.<
 /p><p><br />  Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit yo
 ur instructor and course name when you register if you would like us to no
 tify your instructor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit.
  Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide e
 vidence of your attendance.</p>
