BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/book-mark-story-awards-celebration-yountville?aff=cityspark"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Book Mark Story Awards Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T190000
UID:260904MdpqXhh2b0WmO4w_VafbQg
DESCRIPTION:The challenge is complete\, and now it's time to jubilate! Joi
 n Yountville Arts for the Bookmark Story Celebration on Thursday\, Sept. 2
 4\, from 5:30 to 7 p.m. in the Heritage Room of the Community Center\, 651
 6 Washington Street.\n\nEach writer was a resident\, worker or student in 
 Napa County. Writers submitted one or two unpublished stories in either pr
 ose or poetry format\, with a limit of 60 words per story. A winning story
  connected all elements together\, showing creativity and originality!\n\n
 Submissions were accepted in English from adults or youth age 18 or younge
 r\, or in Spanish from youth age 18 or younger.\n\nYountville Arts\, Napa 
 County Libraries and Friends of the Yountville Library sponsor this event.
  Guests will join the people who support the contest and who will talk abo
 ut why this technique of writing can be useful. Jurors\, who read 39 entri
 es from writers of all ages\, will share suggestions for writing a strong 
 story. And the exciting highlight of the evening is this: You'll hear the 
 winning and honorable-mention stories read by the authors\, along with the
 ir insights into creating micro-compositions. Copies of the bookmarks with
  the winning stories will also be available.\n\n&ldquo\;The Bookmark Stori
 es contest is one of those rare projects that brings every generation toge
 ther through creativity and storytelling. It's inspiring to see how 60 wor
 ds can hold such imagination. We are proud to bring our community's big vo
 ices to appear on small bookmarks\,&rdquo\; project chair Geoffrey Leigh s
 aid.\n\nJoin us for an inspiring and fun evening while you also get the sc
 oop about next year's contest. The celebration is open to the public\, and
  there is no admission charge. We do encourage you to get a free ticket to
  make sure everyone has a seat. Light bites and refreshments will be serve
 d. Arrive early to get a great spot. We look forward to seeing you! \n\nBo
 okmark Stories Contest Thursday\, Sept. 24\, 5:30 to 7 p.m. Yountville Com
 munity Center\n\nFor further information\, contact Katelyn Huss at khuss@y
 ville.com or 707.944.8712
LOCATION:Yountville Community Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/book-mark-story-awards-cel
 ebration-yountville?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
