BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://pheopara.org/jps-backyard-ultra-hike-sept-26-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:JP's Backyard Ultra/Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260812QK01QtkC5kGc-IGCekMGKg
DESCRIPTION:Event Description\n\nJoin us for JP’s Backyard Ultra\, a one
 -of-a-kind ultramarathon and hike set in the scenic trails of Skyline Wild
 erness Park in Napa\, CA. Now in its fourth and final year\, this grassroo
 ts event is more than just a race\, it’s a celebration of life\, resilie
 nce\, and community.\n\nBorn from my personal journey with Stage IV medias
 tinal paraganglioma\, JP’s Backyard Ultra is a fundraiser for the Pheo P
 ara Alliance\, a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit \\(EIN 26-1510652\\) dedicate
 d to empowering patients\, families\, and medical professionals affected b
 y pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma through education\, advocacy\, and gl
 obal support. Learn more at www.pheopara.org.\n\nWhether you’re in it fo
 r one loop or ten\, come run or hike in solidarity\, to honor those facing
  rare diseases\, to challenge yourself\, and to stand as part of a growing
  force for good.\n\n~Jonathan Pascual\n\nThe course features a 3.3 mile lo
 op with 550\\+ feet of climbing\, offering a mix of terrain from steep roc
 ky sections to shaded paths. Scroll down for map below.\n\nParticipants ca
 n choose anywhere from 1 to 10 loops.\n\nRunners and hikers alike start at
  the same time every hour going clockwise on the even hours and counterclo
 ckwise on the odd hours. So it doesn’t matter if you finish your loop fa
 st or slow because everyone starts again at the same time in the next hour
 . Those attempting 10 loops should pace themselves for a final race on the
  10th loop making 33.3 miles. You can do as many or as few loops as you wi
 sh however.\n\nTimed Event: 8:00 AM – 6:00 PM. Please arrive by 0730 for
  course description\, announcement of run prize categories & fundraising p
 rizes.\n\nAid Station: Main camp has various caloric options and drinks wi
 th water only at the bridge and mile 2.3.\n\nFood & Beverages: Provided\, 
 including lunch for participants and volunteers.\n\nCupless Event: Bring y
 our own water bottle or hydration pack. HYDRAPAK\, our Sustainable Racing 
 Partner will provide limited 300 Limited Edition HydraPak Graphic SpeedCup
 s & 8 SpeedFill Pitchers for use at aid stations.\n\nAwards:Medals to all 
 registered hikers and runners.Medal & wine \\(non-alcoholic option for und
 er 21\\) for top three male and female finishers of the 2\, 4\, 6\, 8 loop
 s.Medal\, wine\, and trophy for the fastest 10th loop goes to the top thre
 e male and female finishers and special Vinerunner 4th place trophy.Medal\
 , wine\, and trophy for the fastest cumulative time for 10 loops goes to t
 he top three male and female finishers.\n\nRaffle Prizes: buy tickets on d
 ay of event to win raffle baskets\, gift certificates\, and other special 
 prizes. Proceeds benefit the Pheo Para Alliance.\n\nSilent Wine Auction: p
 lace your bids on exceptional wines generously donated by local Napa Valle
 y wineries\, starting at an unbeatable buy-now price. Proceeds benefit the
  Pheo Para Alliance.\n\nRegistration “Fee”: Donation LinkJP’s Backya
 rd Ultra has always been a free event. Suggested donation to register star
 ts at $30.Participants get a medal\, a variety of snacks and drinks at the
  aid station\, and lunch.To streamline registration\, we are using runsign
 up.com. 100% of suggested starting donation of $30 goes directly to the Ph
 eo Para Alliance. The processing fee of 6% per $1 of transaction \\(cart\\
 ). This fee is charged per transaction\, not per individual participant\, 
 meaning that if a user registers multiple people to a single cart\, the $1
  fee is only charged once\, lowering the overall cost per person.If you ca
 nnot attend or want to donate beyond the suggested amount\, consider givin
 g an additional donation at the donation link.\n\nParking:Do not park at S
 kyline’s main parking lot to avoid parking fee. Parking opens at 0600.Fo
 llow signs for “JP’s Backyard Ultra Parking” for free parking for re
 gistered participants at the Westside parking lot of Skyline Wilderness Pa
 rk.\n\nChildcare: We have volunteers to watch your kids from 0800-1200.\n\
 nPark Rules: No dogs on trails\, stay on marked trails\, carry out your tr
 ash & put in appropriate bins at the main aid station\, trails close at su
 nset.\n\nCamp with us: reservations at Skyline’s Website: Reserve Camp S
 ite. Mention JP’s Backyard Ultra to reserve your spot in our campsite on
  Friday 9/25 & Saturday 9/26. Camping reservation with vehicles is nearby 
 but will be separate from the tent only camping.
LOCATION:Skyline Wilderness Park
URL:https://pheopara.org/jps-backyard-ultra-hike-sept-26-2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
