X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Novel Lovers Of Sebastopol": "https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/315204102/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_novel_lovers_of_sebastopol
X-SOURCE:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County
UID:event_315204102@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041942Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T143000
SUMMARY:The Things We Never Say by Elizabeth Strout [OPTION 2]
DESCRIPTION:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County\, CA\nPublisher's description: A
 rtie Dam is living a double life. He spends his days teaching history to e
 leventh graders\, expanding their young minds\, correcting their casual cr
 uelties\, and lending a kind word to those who need it most. He goes to ho
 liday parties with his wife of three decades\, makes small talk with neigh
 bors\, and\, on weekends\, takes his sailboat out on the beautiful Massach
 usetts Bay. He is\, by all appearances\, present and alive. But inside\, A
 rtie is plagued by feelings of isolation. He looks out at a world gone mad
 —at himself and the people around him—and turns a question over and ov
 er in his mind: How is it that we know so little about one another\, even 
 those closest to us?\n\nAnd then\, one day\, Artie learns that life has be
 en keeping a secret from him\, one that threatens to upend his entire worl
 d. Once he learns it\, he is forced to chart a new course\, to reconsider 
 the relationships he holds most dear—and to make peace with the mysterie
 s at the heart of our existence.\n\nElizabeth Strout\, as we have come to 
 expect\, delivers a moving exploration of the human condition—one that b
 rims with compassion for each and every one of her indelible characters. W
 ith exquisite prose and profound insight\, *The Things We Never Say* takes
  one man’s fears and loneliness and makes them universal. And in the sam
 e breath\, captures the abiding love that sustains and holds us all.\n\n"I
  haven't enjoyed a Strout book this much in years. Strout takes you inside
  Artie\, gradually revealing pieces of his past and his relationships. Des
 pite the premise\, much of the book is upbeat\, and when it isn't\, we're 
 rooting for Artie." - Joan\n\n"More wonderful characters and interesting n
 arrative from Strout. Highly recommend." - Dave\n\n"I too\, am a fan of *T
 he Things We Never Say.* I was immediately drawn into this novel. Can't wa
 it!"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/315
 204102/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260610T221110Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T221110Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108760658?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Anni Piper
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
UID:260903VFKsdS7iD0qogVVv9figFQ
DESCRIPTION:“Piper has the kind of voice that lulls men to their doom. I
 t’s soft and sweet \n\nwhen it wants to be\, scared and vulnerable a mom
 ent later\, then ripping through \n\nyou like a razor… Piper commands so
 ngs utterly.”\n\nJeremy Loome\, The Edmondton Sun\, Canada\n\nOne listen
  will tell you why in her homeland Anni Piper is known as the First Lady o
 f Blues. \n\nNot only is she a sultry vocalist\, but an insightful compose
 r\, accomplished bass player and \n\nshow stopping performer. Born and rai
 sed in Australia\, her passion for blues was ignited by \n\nthe sound of S
 tevie Ray Vaughan. Piper has called the United States home since 2014.\n\n
 ‘Blow Up Doll’ \\(Sugar Daddy Records 2020\\) is the latest release fo
 r Piper and the second on \n\nher own label. Already an internationally ac
 claimed recording artist\, her latest achievement \n\nis becoming a semi-f
 inalist in the 2019 International Songwriting Competition.\n\nPicking up a
  bass guitar at age 14\, Piper completed a Bachelor of Contemporary Music 
 \n\ndegree at 19 years of age. Finding it difficult to resume her performi
 ng career following the \n\nbirth of her son\, Piper recorded her debut al
 bum ‘Jailbait’ in 2004. The all original album was \n\nmeant to be a g
 ood quality demo and wasn’t intended for commercial release.\n\nTo Piper
 ’s surprise\, she was immediately signed to Black Market Music\, Austral
 ia’s most \n\nprestigious blues label and began touring throughout the c
 ountry. The ‘Jailbait’ album won \n\nmultiple awards including Best Ne
 w Talent at the Australian Blues Music Awards\, the ABC \n\nRadio National
  ‘Fresh Air’ contest\, and 2nd place at the Australian National Songwr
 iting \n\nContest.\n\nHer subsequent releases saw her placed as a finalist
  in the Australian Blues Music Awards \n\n\\(Best Female Vocal\\)\, UK Son
 gwriting Contest\, Australian Performing Rights Association \n\nProfession
 al Development Awards\, MusicOz awards and semi-finalist in the Internatio
 nal \n\nBlues Challenge. Piper has earned a reputation as a songwriter of 
 distinction\, her work \n\nhaving a blues sensibility while still addressi
 ng the issues of today.\n\nIn 2008 Piper signed with Blues Leaf Records US
 A \\(Janiva Magness\, Albert Castiglia\\) and \n\nreleased ‘Two’s Comp
 any’\, a compilation of her earlier releases. The album reached \\# 21 o
 n \n\nthe Living Blues chart even though Piper had yet to tour the USA. Sh
 e quickly made up for \n\nlost time and has performed in 45 American state
 s and Canada. Piper has performed to \n\npacked houses at premier venues s
 uch as the House of Blues and BB King’s. She has earned \n\ncritical acc
 laim from publications including Blues Revue and Blues Matters \\(UK\\)
LOCATION:Kelseyville  Pear Festival
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108760658?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
