BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108097027?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
UID:260820LZMtFlxu2k2Ctv1FxaFtuQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Tasting Notes
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108097027?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cimcc.org/gala/", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/california-indian-museum-and-cultural-center-30th-anniversary-gala/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cimcc.org/gala/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:California Indian Museum and Cultural Center 30th Anniversary Gala
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T210000
UID:260812kaL2N0UImUC2ZOywMtmrgA
DESCRIPTION:For 30 years\, the California Indian Museum and Cultural Cente
 r \\(CIMCC\\) has been a vital and unique resource advancing understanding
  of California Indian history\, cultures\, and contemporary leadership. On
  Saturday\, September 26\, 2026\, at 5:00 pm\, CIMCC will celebrate three 
 decades of impact with an anniversary gala —an inspiring evening honorin
 g Indigenous excellence\, celebrating community\, and looking toward the n
 ext generation of Native leadership.\n\nThe event will showcase the richne
 ss\, resilience\, and creativity of Native communities while raising criti
 cal funds to advance CIMCC’s work to preserve and share cultural knowled
 ge\, strengthen intergenerational connections\, empower Native youth and f
 amilies\, and nurture Indigenous leadership for generations to come.\n\nGu
 ests will be treated to an unforgettable Native traditional food dinner pr
 epared by award-winning Chef Justin Pioche\, a 2023 James Beard Award Fina
 list for Best Chef of the Southwest \\(AZ\, NM\, NV\, OK\\) and Food Netwo
 rk Chopped Champion. The evening will also feature a cocktail reception\, 
 silent auction\, inspiring stories of CIMCC’s impact\, and vibrant Nativ
 e entertainment—all set against the beautiful backdrop of Balletto Viney
 ards in Santa Rosa.
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://cimcc.org/gala/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release", "Press Democrat": "https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Chef and Top Chef Alum Chef Nelson German Celebrates Debut Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
UID:260811fg9yPE4BT0uIDyIawZIe6A
DESCRIPTION:PREMO Club Presents "Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release \\+ Din
 ner\n\nYou are invited to join us for an exclusive experience in the heart
  of Sonoma's wine country to celebrate the upcoming book release "Caribbe
 an Cocktails: Drinks & Bites from the Afro-Latino Diaspora"\, \\(June 2\, 
 2026 from Ten Speed Press\\). The book is authored by chef and cocktail cr
 eator Nelson German and James Beard Award–winning culinary writer And
 réa Lawson Gray.\n\nHosted at Aldina Vineyard's Tasting Lounge\,\n\nThe 
 evening begins at 5pm with a cocktail \\+ wine reception featuring herbs\,
  fruits\, and botanicals grown at Little Saint Farm highlighting the farm
 ’s seasonal produce. The evening concludes with an author talk.\n\nThis 
 event is not only a culinary affair\, but also will raise funds for Sprou
 ts Chef Training\, a Bay area-based 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit helping un
 der-resourced youth build careers in the culinary industry. Through culina
 ry training\, mentorship\, and job placement support\, Sprouts equips yout
 h to rise from hardship through culinary training and job placement. Gradu
 ates use these entry-level jobs to kickstart culinary careers\, pay for ed
 ucation\, or pursue new industries.\n\nVisit https://www.sproutscheftrain
 ing.org/ for more information.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
