SUMMARY: Afternoon of East Asian Calligraphy with Christine Renden Haggar
 ty
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Christine Renden Haggarty\nDate: Saturday\, Septe
 mber 26th\nTime: 12:00-3:30PM\nFee: $60.00\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\
 nThe invention of the brush in 300 B.C. revolutionized civilization at th
 e time. Up until then\, people were carving in stone or bone or writing w
 ith sticks in the earth. Because these methods were so slow and unwieldy 
 necessity\, the mother of invention\, the brush was created.\n\nPlease jo
 in Christine for this afternoon of brushwork. You will experience three d
 ifferent types of script – formal\, semi-cursive and cursive and learn to
  write five different characters in those styles. At the end of the class
  you can take your favorite character and write it on a shikishi board.\n
 \nChristine has studied with several different calligraphy masters over 2
 0 years. She has participated in exhibitions around the world\; most rece
 ntly in San Francisco and Healdsburg. She is the Associate Editor of Hear
 t of the Brush\, a collaborative work with Kazuaki Tanahashi\, published 
 in 2016. For more information about Christine go to zenbrush.net http://w
 ww.zenbrush.net/\n\n\nCost for the afternoon is $60 per class with all ma
 terials included. To enroll contact Christine at zenbrush@yahoo.com mailt
 o:zenbrush@yahoo.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Calligraphy,Asian,Brush
