BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/acorn-choir-the-earth-says-awkaf"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Acorn MusEcology Project: The Earth Says
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T163000
UID:6a87318e439f885a0abceb89@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Acorn MusEcology Project is proud to present the Northern Cali
 fornia premiere of Alex Berko's\nSacred Place\n\, an immersive exploration
  of ecological spirituality set to the words of Wendell Berry\, John Muir\
 , William Stafford\, and Rabindranath Tagore. Acorn's 27-voice ensemble wi
 ll be joined by violin\, cello\, and piano to offer up this song cycle of 
 reverential texts within a richly-layered soundscape. Additional original 
 music by co-directors Sarah Dupre and Robin Eschner includes a new setting
  of poetry by the late Steve Fowler\, co-founder of the Sebastopol Peace G
 arden\, soil ecologist\, and community builder. Acorn composer Chris Smith
  will usher listeners into the alchemical mysteries of human composting. J
 oni Mitchell\, Moira Smiley\, and other master songsmiths round out the pr
 ogram. With Acorn's signature approach to melding rich vocal harmony with 
 the values of deep ecology\, this concert will invite reflection on our pl
 ace and purpose on the Earth\, and on the wild intelligence speaking to us
  from beneath our feet.\n"The earth says have a place\; be what that place
  requires\; hear the sound the birds imply and see as deep as ridges go be
 hind each other...Listening\, I think that’s what the earth says."\n– 
 William Stafford.\nLearn more
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/acorn-choir
 -the-earth-says-awkaf
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
