X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Cite It Right with NoodleTools: MLA + APA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T180000
DTSTAMP:20260827T153303Z
UID:20260930T000000Z-23873@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T170000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:This NoodleTools workshop will focus on the MLA + APA citation
  styles. Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style appropri
 ate for your research assignment. When writing a research paper\, the disc
 ipline typically determines the citation style you will use.  In this work
 shop\, you will learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We w
 ill also provide examples to show how to create citations\, create a bibli
 ography and check for errors. There will be time to ask questions at the e
 nd of the overview —bring your sources along. Join us and learn how to c
 ite your sources right!  Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option t
 o submit your instructor and course name when you register if you would li
 ke us to notify your instructor that you have attended the workshop for ex
 tra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way t
 o provide evidence of your attendance.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T180356Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23873-cite-it-right-with-noodleto
 ols-mla-apa
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This NoodleTools workshop will focus on 
 the MLA + APA citation styles. Check with your instructor to confirm the c
 itation style appropriate for your research assignment. When writing a res
 earch paper\, the discipline typically determines the citation style you w
 ill use.</p><p>  In this workshop\, you will learn how to sign up for an a
 ccount with NoodleTools. We will also provide examples to show how to crea
 te citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors. There will be t
 ime to ask questions at the end of the overview —bring your sources alon
 g. Join us and learn how to cite your sources right!</p><p>  Extra Credit:
  As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course na
 me when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that y
 ou have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with you
 r instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.
 </p>
