CATEGORIES:Arts,Museum
DESCRIPTION:Featuring the research and personal collection of author Danie
 l Atkinson\, In the Spotlight: Lawrence's George "Nash" Walker follows the
  career of George "Nash" Walker from Lawrence\, Kansas to the lights of Br
 oadway.&#160\;  Walker and his partner\, Bert Williams\, performed a highl
 y successful vaudeville act on Broadway and overseas\, blazing a trail of 
 opportunity for future Black actors and actresses.This exhibit is funded b
 y a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cu
 ltural Endowment.For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museu
 m Website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/spotlight-george-nash-walke
 r)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T171019Z
LOCATION:Doyle Library\, 1st Floor Lobby - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23088-in-the-spotlight-lawrences-
 george-nash-walker
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Featuring the research and personal coll
 ection of author Daniel Atkinson\, <em>In the Spotlight: Lawrence's George
  "Nash" Walker</em> follows the career of George "Nash" Walker from Lawren
 ce\, Kansas to the lights of Broadway.&#160\;</p><p>  Walker and his partn
 er\, Bert Williams\, performed a highly successful vaudeville act on Broad
 way and overseas\, blazing a trail of opportunity for future Black actors 
 and actresses.<br /><br /><em>This exhibit is funded by a grant from the S
 anta Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Endowment.</e
 m></p><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/spotlight-george-nash
 -walker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, visit the S
 RJC Multicultural Museum Website.</a></p>
