BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/tribute-to-dr-ralph-stanley-with-nathan-stanley-band-and-mission-blue"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Tribute to Dr. Ralph Stanley with Nathan Stanley Band and Mission 
 Blue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T220000
UID:6a4ffbd981edf61b127fc160@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Nathan Stanley Band and Mission Blue honor the King of Mountai
 n Soul\nJoin us for a musical tribute to the one and only Dr. Ralph Stanle
 y!\nLocal bluegrass favorites\nMission Blue\nopen for the touring\nNathan 
 Stanley Band\n.\nYes- Nathan is Ralph Stanley's grandson!\nDon't miss this
  incredible evening of unforgettable harmonies and picking from the legend
 ary musical catalog of Ralph Stanley.\nTickets are $30 GA\, $25 for OCA me
 mbers. Online sales end at 6PM day of show or when sold out. This event wi
 ll be held indoors. ADA seating available\, please email info@occidentalce
 nterforthearts.org to arrange. Beer\, wine\, refreshments available. Art g
 allery open during intermission.\nGet Tickets\nLegendary American bluegras
 s artist\,\nDr. Ralph Edmund Stanley\n\, was internationally known for his
  unique\, innovative style of singing and banjo playing. In 1976\, he was 
 awarded an honorary Doctorate of Music from Lincoln Memorial University\, 
 spawning the popular title “Dr. Ralph Stanley.” He was inducted into t
 he International Music Hall of Honor in 1992\, and the Grand Ole Opry in 2
 000\, the same year in which his work was featured in the film\nO Brother\
 , Where Art Thou?\n- for which he won a 2002 Grammy Award for Best Male Co
 untry Vocal Performance.\nAfter considering retirement and even scheduling
  a farewell tour in 2014\, Ralph Stanley later announced a welcome decisio
 n to continue gracing the country with his beloved\, signature style of mu
 sic.\nOn June 23\, 2016\, Dr. Ralph Stanley passed away while battling com
 plications from skin cancer. He will forever be remembered in the hearts a
 nd minds of his family and fans\, and his legend lives on through his musi
 c\, which will inspire generations of artists to come.\nRead more about Dr
 . Ralph Stanley here\n.\nNathan Stanley is the grandson of Bluegrass Music
  Icon Dr. Ralph Stanley\nand is no exception to the family tradition. Havi
 ng garnered several charting singles in Inspirational Country Music and So
 uthern Gospel Music\, Nathan has come front and center as a music Evangeli
 st.\nThrough decades of performing—spanning the U.S. and international t
 ours—Nathan has achieved numerous milestones. In 2006\, he performed for
  the Queen of England\, and in 2011\, his single “White Dove” (featuri
 ng Vince Gill) reached #1 on the Inspirational country music charts. That 
 same year\, his album “My Kind of Country” was named Classic Country A
 lbum of the Year by the National Traditional Country Music Association.\nR
 ead more about Nathan Stanley.\nMission Blue has quickly become one of Son
 oma County's most beloved bluegrass bands\,\ndelivering their special bran
 d of rhythm\, instrumental craft\, and harmony singing. A deep well of tra
 dition informs Mission Blue’s sets – one can expect songs from the The
  Stanley Brothers\, Larry Sparks\, Bill Monroe\, Flatt & Scruggs\, Mac Mar
 tin and Red Allen\, as well as bluegrass innovators such as J.D. Crowe and
  The New South\, Hot Rize\, Southern Blend and The Johnson Mountain Boys. 
 They also salt each set with reinterpretations of country hits\, folk song
 s and ballads. Based in Sonoma County\, their traditional 5-piece format f
 eatures Dana Frankel on fiddle\, AJ Frankel on guitar\, Sam Reed on banjo\
 , David Thiessen on mandolin\, and Tom Sours on bass fiddle.\nRead more ab
 out Mission Blue.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/tribute-to-
 dr-ralph-stanley-with-nathan-stanley-band-and-mission-blue
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Tockify Rileystreet.Art.Com": "https://tockify.com/rileystreet.art.com/detail/530/1792263600000"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tockify_rileystreet.art.com
X-SOURCE:Riley Street Art Supply
UID:TKF/640bd014795edf4fa3769b14/530/29871060/0/0
DTSTART:20261017T190000Z
DTEND:20261017T223000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/rileystreet.art.com/detail/530/1792263600000
SUMMARY: Afternoon of East Asian Calligraphy with Christine Renden Haggar
 ty
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Christine Renden Haggarty\nDate: Saturday\, Octob
 er 17th\nTime: 12:00-3:30PM\nFee: $60.00\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nT
 he invention of the brush in 300 B.C. revolutionized civilization at the 
 time. Up until then\, people were carving in stone or bone or writing wit
 h sticks in the earth. Because these methods were so slow and unwieldy ne
 cessity\, the mother of invention\, the brush was created.\n\nPlease join
  Christine for this afternoon of brushwork. You will experience three dif
 ferent types of script – formal\, semi-cursive and cursive and learn to w
 rite five different characters in those styles. At the end of the class y
 ou can take your favorite character and write it on a shikishi board.\n\n
 Christine has studied with several different calligraphy masters over 20 
 years. She has participated in exhibitions around the world\; most recent
 ly in San Francisco and Healdsburg. She is the Associate Editor of Heart 
 of the Brush\, a collaborative work with Kazuaki Tanahashi\, published in
  2016. For more information about Christine go to zenbrush.net http://www
 .zenbrush.net/\n\n\nCost for the afternoon is $60 per class with all mate
 rials included. To enroll contact Christine at zenbrush@yahoo.com mailto:
 zenbrush@yahoo.com
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Calligraphy,Asian,Brush
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/640bcf85795edf
 4fa3769ae5/641f7a311421bf7aabc6f378/scaled_384.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Instructor: Christine Renden Haggarty Date: Saturday
 \, October 17th Time: 12:00-3:30PM Fee: $60.00 Location: Santa Rosa Store
  The invention of the brush in...
LOCATION:Rileystreet Art Supply\,103 Maxwell Ct\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95401\,
  USA
