SUMMARY:Standing in Her Power: Portraits Beyond the Colonial Frame
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTSTAMP:20260825T133156Z
UID:20261122T080000Z-23769@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20261122
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,4830,4830/683_Standing_In_Her_Power_-_SRJC_Museum.re
 v.1787260045.png
CATEGORIES:Museum
DESCRIPTION:In early May 2026\, we put out a call for nominations\, asking
  for Native American women to represent their Nations\, their stories\, an
 d their strength through a powerful portrait exhibition celebrating identi
 ty\, cultural legacy\, and the resilience of Native women. Every single en
 try showed us how beautiful and unique and strong Native American women ar
 e.  Two days of photo sessions were held in the Museum in August with phot
 ographer Alexa Treviňo of LexMex Art.This Exhibit is funded by a grant fr
 om the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enric
 hment Endowment.For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum
  website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portraits
 -beyond-colonial-frame)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T173938Z
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23769-standing-in-her-power-portr
 aits-beyond-the-colonial-fr
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In early May 2026\, we put out a call fo
 r nominations\, asking for Native American women to represent their Nation
 s\, their stories\, and their strength through a powerful portrait exhibit
 ion celebrating identity\, cultural legacy\, and the resilience of Native 
 women. Every single entry showed us how beautiful and unique and strong Na
 tive American women are.</p><p>  Two days of photo sessions were held in t
 he Museum in August with photographer Alexa Treviňo of LexMex Art.</p><p>
 <em>This Exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College F
 oundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</em></p><p><a hre
 f="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-
 colonial-frame" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, visi
 t the SRJC Multicultural Museum website.</a></p>
